{
 "id": "roots-world",
 "part": "Δ",
 "el": "Ρίζες του χρόνου, του χώρου και της φύσης",
 "title": "Root families: time, place, earth, light, water, heat, measure, world, nature",
 "level": "A2–C1",
 "intro": [
  {
   "p": "The physical world. Several of these roots are hidden behind an everyday word that looks different: **νερό** but **υδρ-**, **γη** but **γεω-**, **φως** but **φωτ-**."
  },
  {
   "tip": "Each family starts from a root, often in two or three shapes (the present stem, the aorist stem, the ε/ο switch). The Greek verb under the heading is the everyday word that still carries the root; where the everyday word is different (παίρνω for λαμβάνω, γυρίζω for στρέφω) both are given."
  }
 ],
